<title>LEBANON: Lebanon has $337 million BoP surplus in March.</title>
<headline>Lebanon has $337 million BoP surplus in March.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's balance of payments registered a $337 million surplus in March for a cumulative surplus of $564 million in first quarter of 1997, the Bank of Lebanon said on Monday.</p>
<p>This compared with a surplus of $30 million in the first quarter of 1996 and a deficit of $291 million in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 745307 602057</p>
</text>
